sections.append('<p><strong>The generated weaker/stronger groups were too lopsided to answer the moderate-mismatch question:</strong> all neutral control wins were 0% and 100% respectively, and the observed winner never changed across their modifier arms. Seven of 36 copied-club contexts also had all wins or all losses in their small neutral samples. These are finite-sample observations, not mathematical invincibility. A pooled 50.54% copied control obscures the individual disparities. Saturation reduces sensitivity to winner changes and limits comparison with the earlier deliberately competitive pairings. This is a coverage flag, not proof that modifiers are absent, safe everywhere or causing the underlying dominance.</p>')
sections.append('<h2>Copied clubs: ordinary conditions and peak psychology</h2><p>Primary family of four comparisons, with conservative paired intervals protected across that family. Every comparison uses the same fixed copied rosters/tactics and its own neutral control. The pooled control win rate is '+f"{real['cells']['control']['focalWinRatePct']:.2f}%"+'.</p>')
