sections.append('<p>Ordinary ± conditions combine two-match streaks and venue assignments with normal independent thermal traits in three equally weighted moderate laboratory regimes. The design preference of roughly +3–5 points concerns usual full-stack behavior; these inputs omit halftime adaptation and are not a measured distribution of actual season conditions. A small or unresolved ordinary effect is not an instruction to raise coefficients. Peak psychology alone is reviewed against about four points, retaining its uncertainty.</p>')
